    "title": "A CDN for images",
    "body": "Product images are the same for every user and rarely change, but they are large and users are spread around the world. A **CDN** keeps copies on edge servers near users. A user's browser downloads the image from the nearest edge; only when the edge has no copy does it ask the **origin server**. Personal pages, such as a user's orders, are not cached on a CDN.",
